  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Initial Architecture**\n\nOkay, I\'m working on the initial architecture for the Anonymous Real-Time Communication app. I\'ve got an Express server with Socket.IO, listening on port 3000, and integrated with Vite for development and static file serving for production. I\'m focusing on the server component, specifically the `server.ts` file, and trying to flesh out the interaction with the socket layer.\n\n\n**Developing Matchmaking Systems**\n\nI\'m now diving into the time signaling and room engine aspects. I\'ve been detailing the random stranger matchmaking pool, focusing on user queuing with topic interests, instant pairing, and efficient \"next\" handling. I\'m also considering private room codes with encryption and multi-user support, and exploring the WebRTC signaling flow (`offer`, `answer`, `ice-candidate`, `renegotiate`). In addition, I\'m working to define a system for real-time, encrypted-style anonymous chat with features like ephemeral timers and blur spoilers.\n\n\n**Adding Collaborative Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating collaborative features, including a real-time, synced whiteboard with stroke, clear, and undo functionality. I\'m also planning to implement floating reaction emojis and sound triggers. Additionally, I\'m working on a \"chat clear\" event to wipe conversations instantly for both peers. I also have an incognito AI companion endpoint that I will add as an option for icebreakers.\n\n\n**Implementing Anonymity Protection**\n\nI\'m now integrating layers of video filters for enhanced privacy, including options like face blur, cyber hologram, night vision, and pixelation. I\'ve also implemented sound effects for various interactions like incoming calls and message popups. I am working on the `useWebRTC` hook for managing media streams and features like muting and screen sharing, along with the `useSocket` hook for socket connections. Finally, the `Navbar` component, with its stealthy design, is providing active status and a matching toggle, alongside a soundboard button and audio visualizer.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 821016916
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
