  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Invite Link System**\n\nI\'m focusing now on the architecture of invite links, specifically the URL schema. I\'m thinking about how the structure should work for these shareable private rooms, including the base URL, parameters, and encoding. The idea is to build this system with security and user-friendliness in mind.\n\n\n**Refining URL Structure**\n\nI\'ve decided to support multiple link formats: `?room=CODE`, `?join=CODE`, and `/room/CODE`. When the page mounts, I\'ll check `window.location.search` and pathname for the room parameter. If a room code is found, the `roomCodeInput` gets populated, I\'ll switch the active tab to \"custom_room,\" and I\'ll display an \"Invite Link Detected\" notification with immediate options to join or configure settings, to improve UX. I am also working on the Room Link Generation & Sharing Features in the Lobby.\n\n\n**Generating Sharing Options**\n\nI\'m now focused on refining the sharing features. I\'m implementing a one-click \"Copy Invite Link\" for the `?room=ANON-XXXX` format, with visual confirmation. A native Share API option is included for compatible devices. I\'ll also add a QR code generator for easy mobile joining and direct sharing buttons for Telegram, WhatsApp, Twitter, and messaging. In the Active CallView, I\'m integrating a \"Share Room\" button with room code copy functionality and an \"Invite Friend\" modal with all these options, and clear instructions. I\'m also planning to double check the WebRTC connections between peers when joining via link.\n\n\n**Implementing WebRTC Flow**\n\nI\'m now detailing the WebRTC connection flow, starting from the invite link. A \"Waiting for someone\" state displays initially. When someone joins via a link, I\'ll handle `room:joined`, trigger `webrtc.startCall()`, manage SDP offers/answers via a shared code, exchange ICE candidates, and finalize the connection. The system is designed for rejoining and new peers gracefully. I also plan to add UI feedback with sound and visual notifications.\n\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 50220794
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
