    thinking: "**Analyzing the Request Details**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the user\'s request. My focus now is on understanding \"fixx all erorrs\". I\'m meticulously searching for any potential errors, race conditions, or edge cases within the web application components. I am planning to analyze specific components, starting with the web portion.\n\n\n**Developing E2EE Implementation**\n\nI\'m now deep into the implementation details for end-to-end encryption. I\'m focusing on the cryptographic utility, specifically deriving a robust room key using the Web Crypto API, PBKDF2, and SHA-256. The plan includes integrating this key for payload-level E2EE in chat and signaling. This leverages the inherent DTLS-SRTP encryption in WebRTC to ensure security.\n\n\n**Implementing E2EE Encryption**\n\nI\'m now integrating AES-256-GCM with an IV for all in-call chat and data, ensuring only encrypted ciphertext transmits. I\'m also generating a 6-digit cryptographic verification code and SAS security fingerprint using SHA-256 to allow peer cross-verification. To bolster security, I\'m setting up a direct P2P WebRTC DataChannel (e2ee-channel) for server-free chat, alongside a visual E2EE verification modal. I am ready to move to testing.\n\n\n"
