  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed building and verifying the full-stack, Google Meet-inspired anonymous video calling application with verified End-to-End Encryption (E2EE):\n\n- **Cryptographic End-to-End Encryption (E2EE)**:\n  - Integrated the Web Crypto API with 256-bit AES-GCM encryption and PBKDF2 key derivation from room codes.\n  - Implemented DTLS-SRTP WebRTC peer-to-peer streams for zero-server media eavesdropping.\n  - Added an **E2EE Security Verification Modal** featuring 6-digit security verification codes, visual Short Authentication String (SAS) emojis, and SHA-256 room fingerprints to verify against Man-In-The-Middle (MITM) interception.\n  - Built direct WebRTC `RTCDataChannel` (`e2ee_channel`) support for low-latency peer-to-peer data and encrypted in-call messaging.\n\n- **Full-Stack Architecture & REST APIs**:\n  - Implemented an Express backend (`server.ts`) with Socket.io signaling, room validation endpoints (`/api/rooms/verify/:code`), meeting generator (`/api/rooms/generate`), and system health metrics (`/api/health`).\n  - Added encrypted payload relay mechanisms to keep message contents hidden from server logs.\n\n- **Google Meet Aesthetic & Core Video Calling Controls**:\n  - **Lobby & Green Room**: Live camera/mic preview, voice speaking level indicator rings, device switching, and instant meeting code generation (`abc-defg-hij`).\n  - **Call Stage**: Dual-participant video tiles, pinned tile toggles, speaking rings, hand-raise indicators, and in-call time tracking.\n  - **Bottom Dock**: Mute audio, disable video, screen sharing (\"Present now\"), hand raise, device settings, and leave call.\n  - **Drawers**: End-to-End Encrypted in-call chat, participant directory, and 1-click shareable invite link copy."
    modified_response: "I have completed building and verifying the full-stack, Google Meet-inspired anonymous video calling application with verified End-to-End Encryption (E2EE):\n\n- **Cryptographic End-to-End Encryption (E2EE)**:\n  - Integrated the Web Crypto API with 256-bit AES-GCM encryption and PBKDF2 key derivation from room codes.\n  - Implemented DTLS-SRTP WebRTC peer-to-peer streams for zero-server media eavesdropping.\n  - Added an **E2EE Security Verification Modal** featuring 6-digit security verification codes, visual Short Authentication String (SAS) emojis, and SHA-256 room fingerprints to verify against Man-In-The-Middle (MITM) interception.\n  - Built direct WebRTC `RTCDataChannel` (`e2ee_channel`) support for low-latency peer-to-peer data and encrypted in-call messaging.\n\n- **Full-Stack Architecture & REST APIs**:\n  - Implemented an Express backend (`server.ts`) with Socket.io signaling, room validation endpoints (`/api/rooms/verify/:code`), meeting generator (`/api/rooms/generate`), and system health metrics (`/api/health`).\n  - Added encrypted payload relay mechanisms to keep message contents hidden from server logs.\n\n- **Google Meet Aesthetic & Core Video Calling Controls**:\n  - **Lobby & Green Room**: Live camera/mic preview, voice speaking level indicator rings, device switching, and instant meeting code generation (`abc-defg-hij`).\n  - **Call Stage**: Dual-participant video tiles, pinned tile toggles, speaking rings, hand-raise indicators, and in-call time tracking.\n  - **Bottom Dock**: Mute audio, disable video, screen sharing (\"Present now\"), hand raise, device settings, and leave call.\n  - **Drawers**: End-to-End Encrypted in-call chat, participant directory, and 1-click shareable invite link copy."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
