  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Chat System**\n\nI\'m currently focused on designing a chat system that meets the user\'s requirements. The system must support file sharing (images, videos, etc.) and automatically delete chat history after one month. I\'m prioritizing functionalities that are requested by users.\n\n\n**Defining Message Schema**\n\nI\'ve fleshed out the `ChatMessage` schema, which includes fields for sender details, message content, timestamps, and attachment information, including expiration dates for auto-deletion. Attachment details include URLs, file types, and sizes, facilitating efficient data management. I also added a \"reactions\" field.\n\n**Implementing Data Persistence**\n\nNow I\'m focusing on the backend persistence strategy, deciding on how to store messages, with a focus on automatic deletion after one month. I\'m exploring persistent storage options and setting up a dedicated upload directory. I\'m also preparing to create the file upload route.\n\n\n**Outlining Endpoint Functionality**\n\nI\'m now outlining API endpoints and Socket.io events to realize data handling. I\'m focusing on defining endpoints for fetching chat history with expiration details, uploading files with a 30-day TTL, deleting messages, and retrieving expiration summaries. Socket events will manage real-time communication: message sending and syncing, typing indicators, reactions, and file sharing. I\'m prioritizing efficient data management, and auto-purging functionality.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 382300860
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
