  planner_response {
    response: "I have resolved the `Failed to get user media: Requested device not found` error across the application:\n\n- **Resilient Media Stream Acquisition**:\n  - Replaced strict `exact: deviceId` constraints with flexible `ideal: deviceId` matching to prevent `OverconstrainedError` and `NotFoundError` when hardware devices are unplugged, missing, or in sandboxed environments.\n  - Added progressive track fallback: if a combined video + audio request fails, the engine attempts individual video and audio device acquisition separately.\n  - Implemented an in-memory silent audio stream fallback so that WebRTC peer connections, DataChannels, and SDP negotiations remain intact even on devices without a physical microphone or webcam.\n\n- **Dynamic Track Re-acquisition**:\n  - Updated audio and video toggle controls to dynamically query and attach tracks on demand when enabled.\n\n- **Defensive Error Handling & UI Status**:\n  - Added guards around `navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia` across voice notes and chat panels to handle device absence smoothly.\n  - Added an informative device notice badge in the Lobby to guide users when no physical camera or microphone is detected."
    modified_response: "I have resolved the `Failed to get user media: Requested device not found` error across the application:\n\n- **Resilient Media Stream Acquisition**:\n  - Replaced strict `exact: deviceId` constraints with flexible `ideal: deviceId` matching to prevent `OverconstrainedError` and `NotFoundError` when hardware devices are unplugged, missing, or in sandboxed environments.\n  - Added progressive track fallback: if a combined video + audio request fails, the engine attempts individual video and audio device acquisition separately.\n  - Implemented an in-memory silent audio stream fallback so that WebRTC peer connections, DataChannels, and SDP negotiations remain intact even on devices without a physical microphone or webcam.\n\n- **Dynamic Track Re-acquisition**:\n  - Updated audio and video toggle controls to dynamically query and attach tracks on demand when enabled.\n\n- **Defensive Error Handling & UI Status**:\n  - Added guards around `navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia` across voice notes and chat panels to handle device absence smoothly.\n  - Added an informative device notice badge in the Lobby to guide users when no physical camera or microphone is detected."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
