    thinking: "**Examining Fetch Guard**\n\nI\'m now investigating `index.html` as the ideal location for a `fetch` polyfill or guard, specifically within the `<head>` to ensure early implementation. I\'m considering scenarios where `window.fetch`, `fetch` on `window`, or `Window.prototype.fetch` might be compromised in environments like the AI Studio preview iframe or sandboxed browsers.\n\n\n**Analyzing Fetch Redefinition**\n\nI\'ve been exploring how to make `window.fetch` safely writable and configurable. I\'m focusing on a strategy that defines `fetch` with a getter and setter, allowing redefinition without throwing a `TypeError`. The plan involves an immediately invoked function expression to capture the original `fetch` and manage updates to a `_currentFetch` variable. This approach aims to address potential conflicts from extensions or scripts modifying `fetch` in the iframe environment.\n\n\n"
