    response: "I have conducted a comprehensive code audit and resolved the bugs across the WebRTC signaling lifecycle, media handling, and real-time room communication:\n\n- **WebRTC Track & Transceiver Management**:\n  - Pre-allocated audio and video transceivers (`sendrecv`) during peer connection initialization, ensuring that enabling the microphone, camera, or screen sharing dynamically will reliably replace tracks via senders and transceivers without renegotiation drops.\n  - Hardened ICE candidate exchange with filtering against empty or malformed candidate payloads and ensured buffered candidates drain immediately upon remote description settlement.\n\n- **Audio Echo & Cross-Browser Playback**:\n  - Muted the remote video element inside the video grid to eliminate acoustic phasing and echo when playing alongside the dedicated audio element.\n  - Refactored the persistent background audio element to remain in the layout with transparent non-blocking styles, preventing audio decode pausing in WebKit and mobile browsers.\n\n- **Media Recording & Cancellation**:\n  - Fixed voice note cancellation in both the active call chat and lobby room hub so that cancelling an in-progress recording discards audio chunks and shuts down microphone hardware tracks rather than attaching 0-byte files.\n  - Added dedicated recording indicator and cancel/done controls to the Room Chat & File Hub.\n\n- **Auto-Sync & Referrer Protection**:\n  - Implemented automatic background polling for the Lobby Room Chat & File Hub so participants viewing historic or current room data receive updates in near real-time.\n  - Enforced `referrerPolicy=\"no-referrer\"` across all attachment photo previews and media viewers."
    modified_response: "I have conducted a comprehensive code audit and resolved the bugs across the WebRTC signaling lifecycle, media handling, and real-time room communication:\n\n- **WebRTC Track & Transceiver Management**:\n  - Pre-allocated audio and video transceivers (`sendrecv`) during peer connection initialization, ensuring that enabling the microphone, camera, or screen sharing dynamically will reliably replace tracks via senders and transceivers without renegotiation drops.\n  - Hardened ICE candidate exchange with filtering against empty or malformed candidate payloads and ensured buffered candidates drain immediately upon remote description settlement.\n\n- **Audio Echo & Cross-Browser Playback**:\n  - Muted the remote video element inside the video grid to eliminate acoustic phasing and echo when playing alongside the dedicated audio element.\n  - Refactored the persistent background audio element to remain in the layout with transparent non-blocking styles, preventing audio decode pausing in WebKit and mobile browsers.\n\n- **Media Recording & Cancellation**:\n  - Fixed voice note cancellation in both the active call chat and lobby room hub so that cancelling an in-progress recording discards audio chunks and shuts down microphone hardware tracks rather than attaching 0-byte files.\n  - Added dedicated recording indicator and cancel/done controls to the Room Chat & File Hub.\n\n- **Auto-Sync & Referrer Protection**:\n  - Implemented automatic background polling for the Lobby Room Chat & File Hub so participants viewing historic or current room data receive updates in near real-time.\n  - Enforced `referrerPolicy=\"no-referrer\"` across all attachment photo previews and media viewers."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
